Box 54881 (Lika's real phone, 12 Oct 13:58Z): asked about a person outside
her contacts, the run's web_search had the person's public LinkedIn page in
its five results; the reply gave the link and said the current position
could not be confirmed. The second question read the same page.

Misho's choice A (§134, 15:16 UTC): when a public LinkedIn profile is among
the top three results, the server reads that one page (one Tavily extract,
recorded in the cost ledger) and hands it over in the same result as
public_profile {url, read_on, content}. No profile, no read; a failed or
empty read leaves the result as it was. No model-facing text.

Also: §134 recorded; the 4126 scope notes the tester's answer to Q1/Q2
(„Yes to both, it's already in T4126").

